  "reconstructionNotes": "LAYOUT: this is an extremely wide 18-column figure, so call setUiLayout to dock the control panel BELOW the figure (collapsible), never to the right — the SVG must own the full inline width so that at step 0, with the tour on 'Full table', the view is a drop-in replacement for the static textbook image. TYPOGRAPHY HIERARCHY (the previous version read too small when scaled): title largest; element symbols/charges next, sized to nearly fill each cell; 'Group' and 'Period' axis words and the '*'/'**' f-block markers noticeably larger than before and comparable to the symbol size; group/period numbers smallest of the labeled text. Trim the SVG viewBox margins tight around the grid so no width is wasted, and let the grid scale to the container. GRID: 7×18 rounded squares on white with the detached 14-wide f-block centered below, linked by a curved red arrow from a red-outlined box around the group-3 cells of periods 6 and 7. FILLS (pastel): Group 1 pale purple, Group 2 pale green, d-block pale tan, anion nonmetals salmon-pink, Group 17 pale lavender-blue, Group 18 cyan, everything else white. Period-6 correction: shade the group-16 cell (Po) salmon and leave the group-15 cell (Bi) white. LEGEND: condense to small color chips with one-word captions laid out in one or two wrapped rows under the f-block — no tall text column. The clicked-element readout lives in the docked bottom panel and stays under three short lines (e.g. 'Na  sodium  →  Na+   [Ne]3s¹ → [Ne]   loses 1 e⁻ to match neon'). The group slider paints a translucent yellow band over the chosen column with a short caption of that group's typical charge. Tour states dim irrelevant cells to ~20% opacity and reveal the 'charge = group number' / 'charge = group number − 18' callouts."
